{
  "header": [
    "UNALLOCATED — SHOULD — a peer constructing an entity leaves an unset optional field absent rather than null.",
    "",
    "Batch 3. §1.3's SHOULD. A WARN, never a gate. No §9.2 row."
  ],
  "id_status": "unallocated",
  "under": "",
  "title": "In entities the peer constructs, a §3-declared optional field with no value is absent, not present with null",
  "spec": "ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL §1.3 ('Optional fields: SHOULD be absent (key not present) rather than present with a null or zero value when constructing new entities.')",
  "spec_also": [
    "§1.3 ('Absent key and null key produce different bytes and different hashes.')",
    "§3.6 'Optional field defaults' table"
  ],
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.21",
  "level": "SHOULD",
  "profile": [
    "core"
  ],
  "surface": "wire",
  "status": "draft",
  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F27",
  "reading": [
    "§1.3: \"Optional fields: SHOULD be absent (key not present) rather than present with a null or zero value",
    "when constructing new entities. Absent key and null key produce different bytes and different hashes.",
    "However, the presence of an optional field with a null or zero value is semantically valid\".",
    "",
    "WHY A SHOULD GETS A FILE. Two independently built peers constructing the \"same\" capability for the same",
    "grantee produce different content hashes if one writes `expires_at: null` and the other omits it. §1.3's",
    "note says cross-implementation comparison of independently constructed entities \"is not a protocol goal\",",
    "which is why this is SHOULD — but the cost lands on dedup and on any conformance comparison across the",
    "cohort, and a WARN is how it becomes visible.",
    "",
    "\"NULL OR ZERO\". The SHOULD names both. Only NULL is asserted: a zero can be a meaningful value",
    "(`max_delegation_depth: 0` means \"cannot delegate\", which differs from absent = \"unrestricted\", §3.6's",
    "defaults table). Flagging zeros would warn on correct entities. Zeros are witnessed.",
    "",
    "SCOPE. Only fields §3 declares `optional: true`, in entities the peer CONSTRUCTS (handshake responses,",
    "its minted grant). Relayed entities are §1.8's and must keep their nulls (§1.3: \"MUST preserve it when",
    "forwarding\")."
  ],
  "preconditions": {
    "grants": [],
    "identities": [
      "caller"
    ],
    "handlers": [],
    "posture_axes": [
      "seed_policy"
    ]
  },
  "arm": [
    {
      "name": "absent-not-null",
      "kind": "conformant",
      "given": "a completed handshake; every peer-constructed entity of a §3 type the suite knows",
      "why": "§1.3's SHOULD. A null optional is a WARN.",
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "connect",
          "capture": "handshake"
        }
      ],
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "no_declared_optional_field_is_null",
          "capture": "handshake",
          "why": "per §3 type definition; undeclared (extra) fields are not optional fields and are out of scope."
        }
      ],
      "witness": [
        {
          "field": "zero_valued_optionals",
          "why": "recorded, never warned: a zero may be the meaningful value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "control",
      "kind": "negative-control",
      "given": "the assertion applied to a fixture token carrying `expires_at: null`, and to a fixture token carrying `max_delegation_depth: 0` inside delegation_caveats",
      "why": "MANDATORY ANTI-VACUITY, suite-side: the null fixture must fail; the zero fixture must NOT — proving the check does not over-read 'null or zero'.",
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "replay_fixture",
          "fixture": "token with a null optional (must fail); token with a zero-valued optional (must pass)",
          "capture": "fixture"
        }
      ],
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "no_declared_optional_field_is_null",
          "capture": "fixture",
          "expect": "fails on the null fixture; passes on the zero fixture"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "non-conformant-witness",
      "kind": "non-conformant",
      "given": "a peer serializing from a struct with every optional field emitted",
      "expect": "its minted tokens hash differently from a byte-for-byte-equivalent token minted by a peer that omits unset fields",
      "why": "the divergence the SHOULD exists to minimise."
    }
  ],
  "notes": {
    "peer_attributable": true,
    "oracle_check": ""
  }
}
